# Source art the game never loads at runtime: the originals the derived assets
# were cut from, and the PLAY sprite the CSS buttons replaced. They stay in the
# repo so assets can be recut, but there is no reason to ship ~7 MB of them.
#
# NOTE: the goat frames and the audio ARE shipped. They are referenced by name
# at runtime ('assets/art/' + name), so a text search of the source wrongly
# reports them as unused. Do not add them here.
*/assets/art/banner.png
*/assets/art/pannel.png
*/assets/art/counter.png
*/assets/art/score.png
*/assets/art/hand.png
*/assets/art/touch.svg
*/assets/art/play button sprite.png
*/assets/art/verticalfence*
*/assets/art/btn-play-*.png
# The supplied goat and fence sheets, before the keyed matte was cleaned off
# them. Kept so the sprites can be recut; the cleaned sheets are what ships.
*/assets/art/goat-sprite*
*/assets/art/fence-ui*
*/assets/goat/*.raw.png
# The single-sheet celebration goat, superseded by the eleven separate poses the
# mascot controller animates. Nothing references it any more; 1.75 MB.
*/assets/goat/goat-celebration.png

# Loose source art at the repo root. The leading slash anchors the pattern
# there: `assets/` is also the name of the folder inside lab/, and the only one
# that should ever be skipped is this top-level pile of originals.
/assets/

# Test harnesses, never deployed. Named ones were listed one by one, which meant
# every new probe had to remember to add itself - and __qa-main.js was already
# sitting in the bundle because nobody had. Anything with the double-underscore
# prefix is a harness by convention, so the prefix is what is matched.
**/__*

.git/
